{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"clay-nutty-housefly","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# Finish ADR 0056: extract build_agent_kwargs and the telemetry block from run()\n\nDiscovered while executing story 7f86 (decompose `PydanticAIRunner.run()`). Its plan review\n(BLOCK, 3 blocking findings, all the same root) established that 7f86's three children do NOT\nreach the end state ADR 0056 projects. This ticket carries the remainder so it is tracked rather\nthan silently dropped.\n\n## The gap, measured\n\nADR 0056 decision 3 names FOUR extractions:\n\n    interpret_failure(exc, *, run_messages, req_limit, eff_max_iter, ...) -> Never   e6bd  DONE\n    build_model_settings(cfg, req, caps, resolved, *, model_override) -> dict        8229\n    build_usage_limits(cfg, req, UsageLimits) -> tuple                               8229\n    build_agent_kwargs(cfg, req, tools, toolsets, model_settings, ...) -> dict       NOT COVERED\n\nStory 7f86's children cover the first three only. Its own arithmetic lands runner.py at ~620 LOC\nwith `run()` at ~250 lines. ADR 0056's projected end state is ≈470 on the cc33 base with `run()`\nat 60–90 lines. So roughly 150 file lines and roughly 160 method lines are unaccounted for by any\ndescribed extraction — which is exactly what 7f86's plan review flagged as blocking, and why\n7f86's AC2 was corrected downward to the bound its own children reach.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `build_agent_kwargs` — the fourth ADR-named extraction.\n- The ~19-line post-call telemetry block (the success-path `logger.info` with step-usage counters),\n  which ADR 0056's Consequences section calls out by name as a reason the earlier ~250/~15\n  projection was wrong.\n- Destination is the existing runner cluster (`structured_run.py` or a sibling already split from\n  `runner.py`) — NOT a new sub-100-LOC file, which AGENTS.md forbids.\n\n## Constraints inherited from 7f86 (do not rediscover these)\n\n- `Verified` is cast PER PATCHSET (`.github/workflows/gerrit-verify.yaml` checks out the exact\n  `refs/changes/NN/NNNN/P`), so this change must independently leave runner.py under the 700\n  headroom guard and under the 800 hard cap.\n- Comment wording in `run()` may be tightened, but a measured number, a `file:line` citation, a\n  bug/story/epic id, a named failure mode, or a stated invariant must NEVER be dropped to make room\n  under a size guard. That is the \"raise the cap\" anti-pattern wearing a different hat.\n- The `monkeypatch.setattr(runner_mod, \"...\")` hazard is LIVE for this ticket in a way it was not\n  for e6bd: `_pai_model`, `_local_proxy_bypass_base_url`, `cache_settings_for`, `capabilities_for`\n  and `ProviderSession` all sit in the pre-call region this work moves. A `setattr` patch rebinds\n  `runner`'s global while an extracted function resolves through its OWN module globals, so\n  re-importing the name back into `runner` does NOT fix those patches. Each repoint lands in the\n  same commit as its extraction and is named in the commit message with its reason.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `build_agent_kwargs` is extracted as a plain function with explicit parameters (a carrier only\n      if the signature exceeds ~6 parameters, per ADR 0056)\n- [ ] the post-call telemetry block is extracted\n- [ ] `runner.py` and `PydanticAIRunner.run()` LOC are recorded before/after in the commit message,\n      and the change independently leaves runner.py under 700\n- [ ] every monkeypatch repoint lands in the same commit and is named in the message with its reason\n- [ ] the full suite passes with no test ASSERTION weakened, skipped or deleted\n- [ ] no comment lost a measured fact (see Constraints)","id":"5e75-522e-70d1-4363","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Finish ADR 0056: extract build_agent_kwargs and the telemetry block from run()"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785515600993642001,"uuid":"e0bdb2c4-a76f-4795-98bd-84c9a496b3b3"}